<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38470" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">proclāmātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>f</i> [proclamo]. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen., <i>a calling out</i>, <i>crying out</i>, <i>outcry</i>
			(post-class.), <i><span class="en">Quint. Decl. 8, 21</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trux,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 18, 16</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			partic., <i>an appeal</i> to a judge to assert one's
			liberty, <i><span class="en">Dig. 40, 12, 25</span></i>; <i><span class="en">14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">34</span></i>; 23.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
